# =============================================================================
# CitOmni - robots.txt (PRODUCTION)
#
# PURPOSE
#   Provide a safe, application-neutral production default that permits crawling.
#   Application-specific crawl restrictions and sitemap declarations belong to the app.
#
# THREAT MODEL
#   - Avoid framework-level rules that accidentally hide valid application content.
#   - Avoid assuming routes, query parameters, or sitemap locations that an app may
#     not implement.
#
# BEHAVIOR
#   - The empty "Disallow" rule imposes no crawl restrictions.
#   - Applications may add explicit Allow/Disallow rules when their URL structure
#     requires them.
#
# NOTES
#   - Add a Sitemap directive only when the application actually exposes a sitemap.
#   - Sitemap URLs must be absolute.
#   - robots.txt controls crawling, not authorization or confidentiality.
# =============================================================================


User-agent: *
Disallow:
